config DRM
    tristate "DRM/KMS graphics"
    default y
    help
      Linux DRM/KMS with VMware SVGA II and optional VirtIO-GPU backends.
      The VMware function is bound by the boot framebuffer; VirtIO uses
      modern PCI discovery. Selecting M builds drm.ko. Device discovery
      and publication occur when the module loads;
      the early framebuffer and console remain permanent kernel services.
      Open card/PRIME descriptors, mappings, asynchronous jobs, resources and
      hardware callbacks retain the exact module until safely retired.

config DRM_VIRTIO_GPU
    bool "VirtIO-GPU 2D and VirGL DRM/KMS"
    depends on DRM && VIRTIO_PCI
    default y
    help
      Modern VirtIO PCI GPU support, Linux VirtGPU GEM/ioctls, KMS,
      hardware cursor and VirGL rendering with an unmodified Mesa driver.
      Included in drm.ko when DRM is modular. Venus and host-visible blob
      resources are not advertised by this configuration.
